        "original_id": "dfc6981c-47f9-5330-84e9-e393e4d77e7e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincas Kudirka, Jonas Basanavičius\n- Products: Tautiška giesmė, Lithuanian National Anthem\n- Events: Lithuanian National Revival\n- Topics: Lithuania, Lithuanian state, Lithuanian people\n\nFacts:\n- Vincas Kudirka was born on 31 December 1858 and died on 16 November 1899.\n- Vincas Kudirka was a Lithuanian poet and physician.\n- Vincas Kudirka wrote both the music and lyrics of the Lithuanian National Anthem, \"Tautiška giesmė\".\n- Tautiška giesmė is the national anthem of Lithuania.\n- Tautiška giesmė is also known by its opening words \"Lietuva, Tėvyne mūsų\" and as \"Lietuvos himnas\".\n- The fifty-word poem of Tautiška giesmė condensed Vincas Kudirka's conceptions of the Lithuanian state, the Lithuanian people, and their past.\n- Vincas Kudirka and Jonas Basanavičius were among the most active participants in the Lithuanian National Revival.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
